 "response": "**Getosti's current budget is $2095K.**\n\nUnder the policy, only Finance Office entries change the budget, so every other message was ignored. That includes the Sales, PMO, Engineering, Facilities and Vendor items, whether they were rumours or target figures.\n\nThe working had three parts:\n\n1. **Starting point.** #0001 sets the budget at $1730K. Every later Finance Office increase or decrease is then applied in order.\n\n2. **Withdrawal chains.** Each chain was traced back from its last link, because a withdrawal only counts if it has not itself been withdrawn. Some examples:\n   - #0002 still applies. Withdrawal #0161 cancels #0081, so #0032 stands. #0032 cancels #0015, so #0009 stands, which cancels #0007.\n   - #0003 is withdrawn. Withdrawal #1164 cancels #0154, so #0021 stands. #0021 cancels #0013, so #0012 stands, which withdraws #0003.\n   - The same check decided the other disputed updates. #0071, #0051, #0052, #0028, #0093, #0201, #0236, #0275, #0414, #0712 and #0049 still apply. #0006, #0020, #0022, #0033, #0036, #0206, #0384, #0533 and #0568 are withdrawn.\n\n3. **Running total.** All Finance Office changes that remain in effect were applied once each, in order, giving $2095K. The total was worked through once and not independently rechecked.\n\nANSWER: $2095K",
